# Feedback Capture

Use this Rule in every SmartFlow workspace. It defines when the agent proactively offers to report a workflow deviation to the SmartFlow Confluence feedback hub via the `smartflow-feedback` Skill — and, just as important, when it stays silent.

## Trigger Moments

Offer a report only when a step of the current run **demonstrably deviated from what a bundled Skill or Rule promises**. Qualifying deviations:

- a workflow Skill classified the work wrongly and the run had to be re-routed,
- a hard stop that a Skill or Rule mandates was missed or fired at the wrong point,
- the user had to manually correct something the workflow should have done correctly,
- a bundled reference (tool name, catalog entry, template shape) was demonstrably wrong at runtime.

The reference point is always the Skill's or Rule's own text. Ordinary iteration (CSS tweaks, expected preflight stops, user preference changes, external failures like a down server or an unauthenticated MCP) is not a deviation.

## The Offer

At the **hand-over point** of the run — commit hand-over, final report, or the moment the user ends the task — add exactly one sentence, German in a German-speaking session:

> "Schritt X lief schief und wurde korrigiert — soll ich das melden? Report ist vorbereitet."

On yes: run the `smartflow-feedback` Skill with session autofill (the session holds both the failure and the working fix — that is the report material). On no or no reaction: drop it without comment.

## Annoyance Guards (Hard)

- **Only real detected deviations.** Never offer speculatively, never "just in case", never to appear thorough.
- **One sentence.** No pre-built report dump in chat, no multi-line pitch.
- **Never blocking.** The offer never delays the hand-over, never becomes a confirmation gate, and the run result never depends on the answer.
- **Never mid-run.** Deviations noticed during the run are remembered and offered once at the hand-over point, not when they happen.
- **Once per deviation.** A declined offer is not repeated in the same session; several deviations in one run become one combined offer.
- **Never auto-report.** Without an explicit yes, nothing is written to Confluence.

## Manual Path

Reporting works anytime without a trigger: the user can invoke `/smartflow-feedback` for bugs, questions, ideas, and skill/rule proposals. When a user aborts a broken run, the stopped chat itself is the reporting place — the report is made there before moving on, because only that chat holds the session context for autofill.
